          %h2#SpectralSequences
            %strong Interlude) Spectral sequences
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            This section is at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+I"} Introduction to Stable homotopy theory – I
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#part_2_adams_spectral_sequences
            %strong Part 2) Adams spectral sequences
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            This section is at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+2"} Introduction to Stable homotopy theory – 2
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#ComplexOrientedCohomology
            %strong Seminar) Complex oriented cohomology
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            This section is at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+S"} Introduction to Stable homotopy theory – S
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %hr/
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#References References
          %h3#basic_reading Basic reading
          %p
            For
            %strong Prelude) Classical homotopy theory
            a concise and self-contained re-write of the proof (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen67"}> Quillen 67
            ) of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Hirschhorn15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Hirschhorn"}> Philip Hirschhorn
              ,
              %em The Quillen model category of topological spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1508.01942"}> arXiv:1508.01942
              ).
          %p
            For general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            theory a decent concise account is in
          %ul
            %li#DwyerSpalinski95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              , J. Spalinski,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+theories+and+model+categories"} Homotopy theories and model categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://folk.uio.no/paularne/SUPh05/DS.pdf"}> pdf
              ) in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ioan+Mackenzie+James"} Ioan Mackenzie James
              (ed.),
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Algebraic+Topology"} Handbook of Algebraic Topology
              1995
          %p
            For the restriction to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
            good sources are
          %ul
            %li#Lewis78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gaunce+Lewis"}> Gaunce Lewis
                ,
                %em Compactly generated spaces
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/MISC/GaunceApp.pdf"}> pdf
                ), appendix A of
                %em The Stable Category and Generalized Thom Spectra
                PhD thesis Chicago, 1978
            %li#Strickland09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Strickland"}> Neil Strickland
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The category of CGWH spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://neil-strickland.staff.shef.ac.uk/courses/homotopy/cgwh.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            For section
            %strong 1) Stable homotopy theory
            we follow the modern picture of the stable homotopy category for which an enjoyable survey may be found in
          %ul
            %li#Malkiewich14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cary+Malkiewich"}> Cary Malkiewich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The stable homotopy category
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "http://math.uiuc.edu/~cmalkiew/stable.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The classical account in (
            %a{:href => "#Adams74"}> Adams 74, part III sections 2, 4-7
            ) is still a good read, but ignore the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+category"}> Adams category
            ”-construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            in sections III.2 and III.3. What we actually do follows
          %ul
            %li#MMSS00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Mandell"}> Michael Mandell
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"} Stefan Schwede
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Model+categories+of+diagram+spectra"} Model categories of diagram spectra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/PAPERS/mmssLMSDec30.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            For the discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
            we pass to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
          %ul
            %li#Schwede12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Symmetric+spectra"} Symmetric spectra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/~schwede/SymSpec-v3.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            For
            %strong Interlude: Spectral sequences
            a discussion streamlined for our purposes is in (
            %a{:href => "#Rognes12"}> Rognes 12, section 2
            ).
          %p
            In
            %strong 2) Adams spectral sequence
            for the general theory we follow
          %ul
            %li#Adams74
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalized+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalized homology
            %li#Bousfield79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aldridge+Bousfield"}> Aldridge Bousfield
                , sections 5 and 6 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The localization of spectra with respect to homology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.uio.no/studier/emner/matnat/math/MAT9580/v12/undervisningsmateriale/bousfield-topology-1979.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            For the special case of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+Adams+spectral+sequence"} classical Adams spectral sequence
            we follow (
            %a{:href => "#Kochman96"}> Kochman 96, chapter V
            ).
          %p
            For the
            %strong Seminar on Complex oriented cohomology
            an excellent textbook to hold on to is
          %ul
            %li#Kochman96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Kochman"}> Stanley Kochman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bordism%2C+Stable+Homotopy+and+Adams+Spectral+Sequences"} Bordism, Stable Homotopy and Adams Spectral Sequences
          %p
            Specifically for
            %strong S.1) Generalized cohomology
            a neat account is in:
          %ul
            %li#AguilarGitlerPrieto02
              Marcelo Aguilar,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Gitler"} Samuel Gitler
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic topology from a homotopical viewpoint
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://tocs.ulb.tu-darmstadt.de/106999419.pdf"} toc pdf
          %p
            For
            %strong S.2) Cobordism theory
            an efficient collection of the highlights is in
          %ul
            %li#Malkiewich11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cary+Malkiewich"}> Cary Malkiewich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Unoriented cobordism and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mi O
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M O
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.uiuc.edu/~cmalkiew/cobordism.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            except that it omits proof of the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leray-Hirsch+theorem"} Leray-Hirsch theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+spectral+sequence"} Serre spectral sequence
            and that of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+isomorphism"} Thom isomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kochman96"} Kochman 96
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AguilarGitlerPrieto02"} Aguilar-Gitler-Prieto 02, section 11.7
          %p
            For
            %strong S.3) Complex oriented cohomology
            besides (
            %a{:href => "#Kochman96"}> Kochman 96, chapter 4
            ) have a look at
            %a{:href => "#Adams74"} Adams 74, part II
            and
          %ul
            %li#Lurie10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , lectures 1-10 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chromatic+Homotopy+Theory"} Chromatic Homotopy Theory
          %p (These overlap, pick the one that seems more inviting on first reading.)
          %h3#further_reading Further reading
          %p The two originals
          %ul
            %li#Quillen67
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
                ,
                %em Axiomatic homotopy theory
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopical algebra
            %li#Brown73
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Brown"}> Kenneth Brown
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abstract+Homotopy+Theory+and+Generalized+Sheaf+Cohomology"} Abstract Homotopy Theory and Generalized Sheaf Cohomology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1996573"} JSTOR
          %p are still an excellent source. For further reading on homotopy theory and stable homotopy theory a useful collection is
          %ul
            %li#James95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ioan+Mackenzie+James"}> Ioan Mackenzie James
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Algebraic+Topology"} Handbook of Algebraic Topology
              1995
          %p The modern chromatic picture originates around
          %ul
            %li#Hopkins99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"}> Mike Hopkins
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Complex+oriented+cohomology+theories+and+the+language+of+stacks"} Complex oriented cohomology theories and the language of stacks
          %p a useful survey is in
          %ul
            %li#Wilson13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dylan+Wilson"} Dylan Wilson
              section 1.2 of
              %em Spectral Sequences from Sequences of Spectra: Towards the Spectrum of the Category of Spectra
              lecture at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://math.harvard.edu/~hirolee/pretalbot2013/"} 2013 Pre-Talbot Seminar
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/DylanWilsonOnANSS.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p a wealth of details is in
          %ul
            %li#Ravenel86
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Doug+Ravenel"}> Doug Ravenel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Complex+cobordism+and+stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} Complex cobordism and stable homotopy groups of spheres
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/mybooks/ravenelA1.pdf"} pdf
          %p and new foundations have been laid in
          %ul
            %li#LurieHigherAlgebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"} Higher Algebra
        .revisedby
